1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:01,867
<i> Do what I ordered you to do.</i>

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,667
<i>I don't want the risk
of that old woman recovering.</i>

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,800
<i>What happened to my mom?
I don't think I know you.</i>

4
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:08,767
<i>Doc Reyes. I'll go ahead.
Sorry, Ma'am.</i>

5
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:09,967
<i> Who are you?</i>

6
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:11,267
<i> Where am I?</i>

7
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:13,100
<i> Mommy, you're in the hospital.</i>

8
00:00:13,233 --> 00:00:14,467
<i>Don't you really remember
anything?</i>

9
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:17,500
<i> Maybe you can show her things</i>

10
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:20,033
<i>that could bring
her memory back.</i>

11
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,600
<i> Does your head hurt?</i>

12
00:00:22,733 --> 00:00:26,033
<i>If you remember what happened
to you, please tell me.</i>

13
00:00:26,167 --> 00:00:27,933
<i> How's your mom?</i>

14
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:29,367
<i> Has she remembered anything?</i>

15
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:30,333
<i> Not yet.</i>

16
00:00:30,467 --> 00:00:31,733
<i> And you, how are you?</i>

17
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:33,367
<i> Here, imitating you.</i>

18
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,467
<i> You never gave up.</i>

19
00:00:34,633 --> 00:00:36,100
<i> I'm here to support you.</i>

20
00:00:36,233 --> 00:00:37,000
<i> Thank you, Joey.</i>

21
00:00:37,133 --> 00:00:38,633
<i> Amazing, you still have that.</i>

22
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:40,133
<i> I thought I lost it.</i>

23
00:00:40,267 --> 00:00:42,100
<i>That's for you. One each for us.</i>

24
00:00:42,233 --> 00:00:43,667
<i> Lucky you found it.</i>

25
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:45,700
<i>I don't think "luck"
is the word.</i>

26
00:00:45,833 --> 00:00:46,867
<i> What then?</i>

27
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,167
<i> Fate.</i>

28
00:01:06,367 --> 00:01:07,267
[THUDS]

29
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,733
Because of your incompetence,
the problem got worse!

30
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:14,067
Rebecca should have been dead!

31
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:17,333
Berdugo, forgive me.

32
00:01:17,467 --> 00:01:19,233
I'll make it up to you.
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

33
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:21,700
Give me one more chance, Boss.

34
00:01:21,833 --> 00:01:24,000
Your stupidity cannot be
forgiven!

35
00:01:24,133 --> 00:01:27,500
- [GUN FIRES]
- [SINISTER MUSIC PLAYING]

36
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:29,000
Get rid of him!

37
00:01:29,133 --> 00:01:31,400
Or Berdugo will come after you
next.

38
00:01:31,533 --> 00:01:35,967
[SINISTER MUSIC CONTINUES]

39
00:01:37,567 --> 00:01:41,800
If Rebecca really has amnesia,
she should stay that way.

40
00:01:41,967 --> 00:01:44,233
Her memory must not return.

41
00:01:54,233 --> 00:01:55,400
Good morning, Ma'am.

42
00:01:55,533 --> 00:01:57,967
Andrew just stepped out.
I'll call him back.

43
00:01:58,100 --> 00:02:00,033
No!
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:00,167 --> 00:02:01,600
Help me.

45
00:02:02,233 --> 00:02:05,500
My life is in danger.
He will kill me...

46
00:02:05,633 --> 00:02:07,967
He will kill me...

47
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:11,633
I can't tell if the old woman
really remembers nothing.

48
00:02:13,267 --> 00:02:15,400
The timing is too convenient.

49
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:17,633
She suddenly has amnesia now.

50
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:20,867
It could be real,
but she could also recover.

51
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,033
Will you wait
until she remembers?

52
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:26,100
If you want, I'll do it.

53
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,233
Not yet.

54
00:02:28,733 --> 00:02:31,100
Rebecca is surely guarded now.

55
00:02:31,233 --> 00:02:35,400
And besides, Andrew will never
leave her side.

56
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,467
He even hired security.

57
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,000
So, what's your plan now?

58
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:43,300
Ma'am, wait! You're hurting me.

59
00:02:43,433 --> 00:02:45,500
- Ma'am...
- Help me, Clarissa.

60
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:50,333
My life is in danger,
and so are my children's lives.

61
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,667
Help me.

62
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:53,767
Help me, please.
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

63
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:56,833
Ma'am, what are you saying?
Can you remember everything?

64
00:02:56,967 --> 00:02:59,567
Maybe you're just dreaming.
Wait, I'll call the doctor.

65
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:02,733
- No! No!
- I'll just call the doctor...

66
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:04,333
No one must know,

67
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:07,000
not even my children.

68
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:09,967
They'll be in greater danger.

69
00:03:10,100 --> 00:03:11,967
I'm serious, Clarissa.

70
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,133
I'm serious.

71
00:03:13,267 --> 00:03:16,733
Help me. I'm telling the truth,
Clarissa.

72
00:03:16,867 --> 00:03:19,967
- I'm telling the truth!
- Ma'am, it hurts.

73
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:26,200
[REBECCA SCREAMING]
I am going to get the doctor!

74
00:03:27,567 --> 00:03:34,600
Sorry! I didn't recognize her!
I thought she was someone else!

75
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:39,200
[GROANING]

76
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:41,233
Mom, calm down, calm down.

77
00:03:42,367 --> 00:03:44,000
Mom, calm down.

78
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:52,433
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

79
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,867
- [THUDDING]
- [GRUNTING]

80
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

81
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:01,167
Ouch, it hurts!

82
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:03,467
Ouch! My arm got caught.

83
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,333
Sorry, Dad. I got carried away.

84
00:04:05,467 --> 00:04:06,600
That was good.

85
00:04:07,533 --> 00:04:10,833
But, child, what I'm teaching
you is only self-defense,

86
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:12,400
not for showing off, okay?

87
00:04:12,533 --> 00:04:13,467
Yes, Dad.

88
00:04:13,600 --> 00:04:15,533
But what's our next lesson?

89
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:16,900
What next lesson?

90
00:04:17,033 --> 00:04:19,233
You've learned all my moves.

91
00:04:20,200 --> 00:04:22,400
Then let's go to
the firing range.

92
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:24,467
How can I take you
to the firing range?

93
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:26,233
I can't even leave the house.

94
00:04:26,833 --> 00:04:30,900
If we practice firing here,
the neighbors will complain.

95
00:04:31,833 --> 00:04:35,433
Honestly,
I'm so bored here at home.

96
00:04:35,567 --> 00:04:38,233
I don't even know
what's happening with the case

97
00:04:38,367 --> 00:04:39,467
I'm putting up with.

98
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:42,733
Feels like I'll rot here.

99
00:04:42,867 --> 00:04:45,300
[OMINOUS MUSIC]

100
00:04:46,333 --> 00:04:48,100
I'm really sorry.

101
00:04:48,233 --> 00:04:50,633
I didn't think mommy would do
that to you.

102
00:04:50,767 --> 00:04:52,600
It's okay, Ma'am.

103
00:04:52,733 --> 00:04:56,400
That's how patients are
when agitated.

104
00:04:56,533 --> 00:05:01,300
They become violent
and say random things.

105
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,300
Did mommy say something?

106
00:05:03,433 --> 00:05:04,467
Like what?

107
00:05:06,767 --> 00:05:09,467
I may have misheard again.

108
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:15,267
Before you came in,
Ma'am Rebecca seemed different.

109
00:05:15,967 --> 00:05:17,267
What do you mean?

110
00:05:18,467 --> 00:05:22,567
Can someone with amnesia
have a lucid moment?

111
00:05:23,633 --> 00:05:25,433
Mom had a lucid moment?

112
00:05:26,033 --> 00:05:28,900
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:34,100
I'm not sure, Sir Tomas.

114
00:05:34,267 --> 00:05:38,300
Maybe she was just dreaming
and woke up,

115
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:40,933
so she said random things.

116
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,833
That's okay.
Mommy could just be dreaming.

117
00:05:46,967 --> 00:05:49,533
What did mommy say?

118
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:53,667
<i>No one must know,
not even my children.</i>

119
00:05:53,800 --> 00:05:56,100
<i> They'll be in greater danger.</i>

120
00:05:56,233 --> 00:06:02,967
I really couldn't understand,
Sir.

121
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:05,167
Sorry, Clarissa.

122
00:06:06,100 --> 00:06:10,333
Take a break first. Go home.
We'll take care of mommy.

123
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:13,100
I'll call the driver
to take you home.

124
00:06:14,733 --> 00:06:17,600
No need, Ma'am. I'm fine here.

125
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:19,567
Miss Clarissa, please.

126
00:06:19,700 --> 00:06:22,033
Let the driver bring you home.
There's no problem.

127
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:24,933
Honestly,
we're the ones who owe you.

128
00:06:25,967 --> 00:06:29,300
And Joey might get mad at me.

129
00:06:34,267 --> 00:06:35,967
All right, thank you.

130
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:46,633
[STIRRING MUSIC]

131
00:06:52,967 --> 00:06:54,800
[CLACKING]

132
00:06:54,933 --> 00:06:57,067
Sorry, Sir! Sorry, sorry!

133
00:06:58,533 --> 00:07:00,733
Fix it before Liza finds out.

134
00:07:00,867 --> 00:07:01,733
Okay, Sir.

135
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:11,433
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:16,267
<i> We can't just let Jin Ho go.</i>

137
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:19,867
He is dad's only lead
to the syndicate.

138
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,733
Why are we even talking
about this?

139
00:07:23,467 --> 00:07:25,867
Didn't your dad say he
doesn't want you meddling

140
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:27,233
in his investigation?

141
00:07:28,833 --> 00:07:30,833
I knew it,
you're planning something.

142
00:07:30,967 --> 00:07:33,567
No way. Your dad will get mad.

143
00:07:33,700 --> 00:07:36,300
But I want to do this for dad.

144
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:40,233
If we find the syndicate's
hideout as soon as possible,

145
00:07:40,367 --> 00:07:41,967
they'll be caught faster.

146
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:45,167
And our suffering will end,

147
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,500
- especially dad's.
- Wait...

148
00:07:47,667 --> 00:07:48,767
Ours?

149
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:50,467
Why am I included?

150
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,433
You'll be the one calling
Jin Ho.

151
00:07:53,500 --> 00:07:55,400
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

152
00:07:55,533 --> 00:07:57,233
Is there a problem?

153
00:07:57,367 --> 00:08:01,533
It bothered me that this woman's
face looked familiar.

154
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,967
And then I remembered something.

155
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:08,833
Look at this.

156
00:08:08,967 --> 00:08:12,800
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:16,333
You think this could be her?

158
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:21,167
The video is too blurry.

159
00:08:21,333 --> 00:08:25,200
If she's that woman,
it means Jin Ho knows her.

160
00:08:26,233 --> 00:08:28,267
That Korean is betraying you.

161
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:30,800
It's not impossible
he's betraying our group.

162
00:08:32,367 --> 00:08:34,033
Go on.

163
00:08:34,167 --> 00:08:37,133
You know, I can't be the one
to call him.

164
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:39,900
Last time we were together,
the police chased him.

165
00:08:40,033 --> 00:08:41,333
He might suspect something.

166
00:08:41,467 --> 00:08:43,267
I don't know, Joey.
I don't know.

167
00:08:43,400 --> 00:08:45,633
He's our friend, but...

168
00:08:45,767 --> 00:08:48,900
we're quick to think
badly of him.

169
00:08:49,033 --> 00:08:51,533
He's still concerned about us.

170
00:08:51,667 --> 00:08:55,633
He was with me when you
and Andrew left me at Valmora.

171
00:08:56,733 --> 00:08:59,500
And he saved our lives
many times.

172
00:09:00,700 --> 00:09:02,733
But dad has a lot of proof
against him.

173
00:09:04,067 --> 00:09:07,533
And maybe he's just checking
on us because he's spying.

174
00:09:07,667 --> 00:09:09,300
Hey, that's not true.

175
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:11,167
If that's what he was doing,

176
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:13,900
he would've told the syndicate
who you are.

177
00:09:18,167 --> 00:09:19,433
[GUN COCKS]
Which do you prefer?

178
00:09:19,567 --> 00:09:21,900
You take him out or I'll do it?

179
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:23,700
Put that away.

180
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:26,200
It might backfire on you.

181
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,100
If we kill him now,

182
00:09:30,233 --> 00:09:34,033
we won't know his true
connection to that woman.

183
00:09:34,167 --> 00:09:37,267
I want to know first
where this leads us.

184
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,700
Don't worry.

185
00:09:38,833 --> 00:09:40,633
I'll handle this carefully.

186
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:46,100
And, Matias,
this stays between us.

187
00:09:46,233 --> 00:09:49,067
Don't tell Berdugo yet.

188
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:52,933
After all, he's busy with his
family affairs.

189
00:09:53,067 --> 00:09:55,533
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

190
00:09:55,667 --> 00:09:57,200
All right, here's the plan.

191
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:02,767
You call him,
then say we'll meet.

192
00:10:02,933 --> 00:10:05,233
But what we'll really do
is follow him

193
00:10:05,367 --> 00:10:08,333
- to see what he's doing...
- Okay, okay, I'll call him.

194
00:10:08,467 --> 00:10:11,267
If we prove your suspicions
wrong,

195
00:10:11,400 --> 00:10:14,600
would you tell your dad
to stop targeting Jin Ho?

196
00:10:14,733 --> 00:10:16,000
Sure!

197
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:19,300
I'll even apologize to you
for suspecting your "oppa."

198
00:10:19,433 --> 00:10:21,833
- All right! You said it, okay?
- Call him now.

199
00:10:21,967 --> 00:10:22,633
I'm counting on your word
of honor.

200
00:10:22,767 --> 00:10:23,733
Sure!

201
00:10:25,867 --> 00:10:26,933
There.

202
00:10:30,067 --> 00:10:40,033
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

203
00:10:46,967 --> 00:10:55,600
- [PHONE RINGING]
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:10:55,900 --> 00:10:57,167
Nothing, it just keeps ringing.

205
00:10:57,667 --> 00:10:59,033
Text him.

206
00:10:59,167 --> 00:11:00,500
Okay.

207
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:05,200
[PHONE CHIMES]
There, I tried.

209
00:11:05,333 --> 00:11:07,200
I'll just try again later.

210
00:11:09,233 --> 00:11:10,533
[PHONE CHIMES]

211
00:11:10,667 --> 00:11:16,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:11:16,567 --> 00:11:20,433
[PHONE RINGING]

213
00:11:22,967 --> 00:11:25,233
- [SIGHS]
- [OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:11:25,367 --> 00:11:27,467
Why didn't you answer the phone?

215
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,800
Who was it?

216
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:32,867
Just a friend who wants
to meet up, but...

217
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:38,533
I know I can't go out.
That's why I ignored it.

218
00:11:38,667 --> 00:11:42,567
Like I said, I'll do whatever
you want me to do.

219
00:11:42,733 --> 00:11:45,833
If you want me to stay here,
I'll stay.

220
00:11:46,967 --> 00:11:48,500
But you're sulking.

221
00:11:49,433 --> 00:11:52,267
If you want to go see
your friend, go.

222
00:11:54,267 --> 00:11:56,800
I'm worried about Clarissa.

223
00:11:56,933 --> 00:12:00,400
If mommy sees her again,
she might hurt her.

224
00:12:00,533 --> 00:12:02,200
Well, you're right.

225
00:12:02,333 --> 00:12:03,900
I also don't understand

226
00:12:04,033 --> 00:12:07,367
why mommy reacted that way
to Clarissa.

227
00:12:07,500 --> 00:12:11,467
I was thinking not to let her
come here for now.

228
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,433
There are nurses anyway.

229
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:15,333
Wait, you're deciding too fast.

230
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,167
Didn't you think that if mommy's
memories are coming back,

231
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:21,767
then it's better
if Miss Clarissa is here?

232
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:24,300
What if mommy hurts Clarissa
again?

233
00:12:24,433 --> 00:12:26,567
- That's embarrassing!
- But what if she doesn't?

234
00:12:27,267 --> 00:12:31,100
What if Miss Clarissa
could help mommy remember?

235
00:12:31,233 --> 00:12:32,933
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:12:33,067 --> 00:12:35,467
I thought I'm a prisoner here?

237
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:41,867
Yes, but keeping you here
isn't doing me any good.

238
00:12:42,733 --> 00:12:45,333
You always look bored,
you look upset.

239
00:12:45,467 --> 00:12:47,233
And I know you.

240
00:12:47,367 --> 00:12:50,700
You become more reckless
when you're unhappy.

241
00:12:50,867 --> 00:12:53,667
So better if you just do
what you want to do.

242
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:55,500
Just remember to be careful.

243
00:12:57,367 --> 00:12:58,567
I will.

244
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:10,467
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:13:14,967 --> 00:13:16,200
[PHONE CHIMES]
Wait.

246
00:13:17,167 --> 00:13:19,067
Hey, perfect, it's Jin Ho!

247
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:20,833
- Here.
- Let me see.

248
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:23,700
- There, he's just checking in.
- Invite him now.

249
00:13:23,833 --> 00:13:25,567
Tell him we'll meet him.

250
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:28,533
Invite him right away?
Can't we just chat first?

251
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:32,133
Gosh! Even with Jin Ho,
you're shy.

252
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:34,000
You're exaggerating. I'm not.

253
00:13:34,133 --> 00:13:35,533
Of course, I just don't want him
to think

254
00:13:35,667 --> 00:13:38,033
I'm too eager to see him
right away.

255
00:13:38,167 --> 00:13:39,467
You're being dramatic.

256
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:41,067
You'll just text him.

257
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:44,200
Tell him we'll meet,
and Andrew will be there too.

258
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:47,100
So...

259
00:13:47,233 --> 00:13:49,200
The two of you are okay now?

260
00:13:49,333 --> 00:13:51,100
Of course.

261
00:13:51,233 --> 00:13:54,133
And Jin Ho is Andrew's
friend too.

262
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:57,167
And I think it's time
for a reunion.

263
00:13:57,900 --> 00:14:03,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:14:08,433 --> 00:14:09,867
Mom...

265
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,100
Are you okay?
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

266
00:14:11,233 --> 00:14:14,900
Miss Clarissa mentioned you
had a lucid memory?

267
00:14:16,267 --> 00:14:17,767
Are you okay now, Mom?

268
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:19,267
Can you remember anything?

269
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,733
Mom, please tell me.

270
00:14:21,667 --> 00:14:22,667
Mom, please.

271
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:27,067
Mom, so we can find the one
who did this to you.

272
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:30,000
Please, Mom.

273
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:31,400
Is there?

274
00:14:31,533 --> 00:14:32,667
- Andrew.
- Mom...

275
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,033
Don't pressure her.

276
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:35,733
You might get hurt.

277
00:14:35,867 --> 00:14:37,633
Why are you interfering?

278
00:14:39,967 --> 00:14:41,933
Don't you want mommy
to remember?

279
00:14:42,067 --> 00:14:44,833
I you're not going to help,
then stay out of my business!

280
00:14:44,967 --> 00:14:47,067
How dare you talk to me
like that?

281
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:52,900
[TENSE MUSIC]

282
00:14:53,733 --> 00:14:55,167
Hon!

283
00:14:55,467 --> 00:14:57,333
Don't argue with Andrew.
What's going on?

284
00:14:57,467 --> 00:14:58,600
Stop this!

285
00:15:00,433 --> 00:15:03,500
An you, why are you talking
to your brother like that?

286
00:15:03,667 --> 00:15:07,000
He's just concerned with mommy
and the people around him!

287
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,600
I'm sorry.

288
00:15:11,433 --> 00:15:12,533
I'm sorry, Tomas.

289
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:17,300
I just couldn't stop myself.

290
00:15:17,900 --> 00:15:21,167
I was thinking about
what Miss Clarissa told me.

291
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:25,567
I was hoping mom's memory
would return.

292
00:15:26,633 --> 00:15:32,933
Is it really that important
for my memory to come back?

293
00:15:34,667 --> 00:15:38,233
If I can still remember
something, then good.

294
00:15:39,567 --> 00:15:45,333
But for now, be content
that we're together...

295
00:15:46,933 --> 00:15:48,500
that I'm alive,

296
00:15:49,333 --> 00:15:51,700
instead of fighting!

297
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,833
Andrew, please...

298
00:15:56,933 --> 00:15:59,133
Okay, Mom. I'm sorry.

299
00:16:02,167 --> 00:16:03,933
It won't happen again, Mom.

300
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:15,567
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

301
00:16:23,167 --> 00:16:28,900
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

302
00:16:34,233 --> 00:16:35,667
Love...

303
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:37,200
Make a small portion.

304
00:16:37,333 --> 00:16:39,133
Your daughter said
she won't eat here.

305
00:16:39,267 --> 00:16:40,800
She's going out with Peter.

306
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,733
Is that so?
Then let's just eat canned food.

307
00:16:44,867 --> 00:16:47,100
No, finish cooking that.
It's already there.

308
00:16:48,233 --> 00:16:49,967
All right, but wait...

309
00:16:50,867 --> 00:16:53,600
Good to know you allowed
your daughter.

310
00:16:53,733 --> 00:16:56,633
Of course. I'm the only one
under a house arrest,

311
00:16:56,767 --> 00:16:58,133
not the whole family.

312
00:16:58,267 --> 00:16:59,900
That's true.

313
00:17:01,267 --> 00:17:03,433
What's with that?
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

314
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:06,233
Did she hurt you?

315
00:17:07,867 --> 00:17:10,567
Ma'am Rebecca didn't do it
intentionally.

316
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:13,233
She suddenly lashed out earlier.

317
00:17:15,267 --> 00:17:18,300
I don't even understand
what happened.

318
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:21,400
She suddenly asked me for help.

319
00:17:21,533 --> 00:17:24,867
I don't know
if what she said was true.

320
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,233
You know she's not
in her right mind.

321
00:17:28,200 --> 00:17:30,567
-Miguel...
-You shouldn't go there anymore.

322
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,400
She might do something to you.

323
00:17:32,533 --> 00:17:35,933
Miguel, the person is sick.
Try to understand.

324
00:17:36,067 --> 00:17:37,133
Even so!

325
00:17:37,267 --> 00:17:41,167
I can't even go out because
I'm worried about you all.

326
00:17:41,833 --> 00:17:44,200
Listen to me.
I don't want you to get hurt.

327
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:48,000
All right,
I'll talk to Ma'am Yvette.

328
00:17:48,167 --> 00:17:49,967
Just relax.

329
00:17:50,100 --> 00:17:50,967
Don't stress yourself...

330
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,167
Watch your heart.

331
00:17:53,433 --> 00:17:55,067
Are we pushing through
or should we cancel?

332
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,733
No, we're pushing through.

333
00:17:57,433 --> 00:18:00,300
It's just that, Andrew isn't
replying to my texts.

334
00:18:00,433 --> 00:18:01,933
But I'll call him.

335
00:18:02,967 --> 00:18:05,300
Does Andrew really need
to be there?

336
00:18:05,433 --> 00:18:07,667
He might be busy with his mom.

337
00:18:07,800 --> 00:18:09,700
Besides, he's not that close
to Jin Ho.

338
00:18:09,833 --> 00:18:13,667
It's better if we're complete
when we meet Jin Ho.

339
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,400
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]
And we need a better vehicle.

340
00:18:18,533 --> 00:18:21,100
What if something happens?
Can your pick-up handle it?

341
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,200
- Now you're blaming my vehicle.
- The pick-up can't handle it.

342
00:18:26,933 --> 00:18:28,633
I just got carried away earlier.

343
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:31,267
I know.

344
00:18:32,067 --> 00:18:34,433
But Yvette is right.

345
00:18:34,833 --> 00:18:36,467
You're stressed out.

346
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:38,133
Maybe you need a change
of environment,

347
00:18:38,267 --> 00:18:39,467
even for a while.

348
00:18:39,600 --> 00:18:42,533
That's why she asked me
to come here, to be with you.

349
00:18:42,667 --> 00:18:45,900
Maybe I did overreact earlier.

350
00:18:46,033 --> 00:18:51,233
But is it wrong to be emotional
when it comes to my mom?

351
00:18:51,367 --> 00:18:52,933
Definitely not.

352
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:58,333
But it's not good
to put her under pressure.

353
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,867
She's already going through
a lot.

354
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
You're adding to her stress.

355
00:19:04,667 --> 00:19:10,300
Andrew, if Aunt Rebecca
needs time to recover,

356
00:19:10,433 --> 00:19:12,733
you also need a break.

357
00:19:12,867 --> 00:19:14,800
Tell me, when was the last time
you did something

358
00:19:14,933 --> 00:19:16,833
other than watch over your mom?

359
00:19:18,167 --> 00:19:19,667
It's been a while.

360
00:19:20,733 --> 00:19:23,200
Even the<i> Tirada</i> ,
I've been neglecting it too.

361
00:19:23,333 --> 00:19:24,700
Wait, no, no, no.

362
00:19:24,833 --> 00:19:27,033
We're not going to talk
about work.

363
00:19:28,667 --> 00:19:29,967
I know.

364
00:19:30,767 --> 00:19:32,367
Let's go watch a movie,

365
00:19:32,500 --> 00:19:34,633
so you can get your mind
off things. Is that okay?

366
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:36,567
Let's do that?

367
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:39,233
[PHONE RINGING]

368
00:19:39,367 --> 00:19:40,867
Sorry, excuse me.

369
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:47,900
Hello?

370
00:19:48,033 --> 00:19:50,233
Andrew, good thing you answered.

371
00:19:50,367 --> 00:19:51,633
Sorry...

372
00:19:51,767 --> 00:19:55,467
I wasn't checking my messages.
Wait, is there a problem?

373
00:19:55,600 --> 00:19:59,833
Peter and I plan to confront
Jin Ho.

374
00:19:59,967 --> 00:20:01,600
<i> Are you joining?</i>

375
00:20:01,767 --> 00:20:03,233
Yes, sure.

376
00:20:03,367 --> 00:20:05,733
Text me where you are.

377
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:06,933
All right.

378
00:20:07,067 --> 00:20:09,067
Let's go to the meeting place
ahead of him.

379
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:12,533
Then we'll plan how
to corner Jin Ho.

380
00:20:12,667 --> 00:20:14,333
Okay, I'm on my way.

381
00:20:14,467 --> 00:20:16,200
Okay, bye. Take care.

382
00:20:18,267 --> 00:20:19,433
Wait.

383
00:20:19,567 --> 00:20:21,167
You're leaving?

384
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:24,200
Zoey, I'm sorry.

385
00:20:24,333 --> 00:20:26,567
Something really important
came up.

386
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:27,833
I'll make it up to you.

387
00:20:28,967 --> 00:20:30,733
Wait, so you're just leaving me
here?

388
00:20:30,867 --> 00:20:32,167
Sorry.

389
00:20:32,300 --> 00:20:33,900
Andrew!

390
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:42,367
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

391
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:46,700
Jackpot! That's our target.

392
00:20:46,833 --> 00:20:48,833
[CAR REVVING]

393
00:20:50,367 --> 00:20:52,533
Come on, let's follow him.

394
00:20:52,667 --> 00:20:56,500
- [REVVING]
- [BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

395
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:04,233
[WHIRRING]

396
00:21:07,400 --> 00:21:08,800
You're going somewhere?

397
00:21:08,967 --> 00:21:10,900
Yeah, I'm meeting
with my friend.

398
00:21:11,033 --> 00:21:12,067
You're okay with that, right?

399
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,433
Yes, just be careful.

400
00:21:16,633 --> 00:21:24,200
- [WHIRRING]
- [OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

401
00:21:26,200 --> 00:21:36,167
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

402
00:21:40,733 --> 00:21:42,633
[PHONE RINGS]

403
00:21:42,967 --> 00:21:44,067
Joey?

404
00:21:44,300 --> 00:21:46,300
Hello, Andrew?
Are you there already?

405
00:21:46,433 --> 00:21:48,000
<i> I'm here.</i>

406
00:21:48,133 --> 00:21:50,600
I'm just looking for a spot
where we can talk.

407
00:21:50,733 --> 00:21:52,200
<i> We're almost there too.</i>

408
00:21:52,333 --> 00:21:53,767
But there's a problem.

409
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:56,733
<i> Peter's tire burst.</i>

410
00:21:56,867 --> 00:21:58,767
Because you don't even check it.

411
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:02,467
Wow! You have the nerve to blame
and you're not even helping.

412
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:03,767
I'm sorry, okay?

413
00:22:03,900 --> 00:22:07,067
<i>Do you need help?
I can go there.</i>

414
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:08,600
<i> No, it's fine.</i>

415
00:22:08,733 --> 00:22:11,667
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

416
00:22:11,800 --> 00:22:16,300
<i>And it's almost done anyway.
We're going there.</i>

417
00:22:16,467 --> 00:22:20,333
<i>Because after 20 million years,
Peter finally fixed his tire.</i>

418
00:22:20,467 --> 00:22:23,867
<i>- It's fine now, right?
- It's almost done.</i>

419
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:29,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

420
00:22:30,633 --> 00:22:32,267
Joey, wait, okay?

421
00:22:32,400 --> 00:22:42,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

422
00:22:54,767 --> 00:22:57,267
Hello, Joey?

423
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:58,700
Andrew, what's that?

424
00:22:59,900 --> 00:23:02,667
Sorry, Joey,
I thought there was...

425
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:05,733
<i>Andrew, what's happening?
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

426
00:23:07,267 --> 00:23:08,833
Andrew!

427
00:23:08,967 --> 00:23:17,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,733
I have no idea who did this
to my brother.

429
00:23:22,900 --> 00:23:26,233
We both know Andrew has done
a lot of exposés,

430
00:23:26,367 --> 00:23:27,633
so lots of people are angry
with him.

431
00:23:27,767 --> 00:23:29,933
We're just here to visit
Andrew Dizon.

432
00:23:30,067 --> 00:23:32,500
Sorry. Ma'am Zoey gave strict
orders.

433
00:23:32,633 --> 00:23:33,667
No one can enter.

434
00:23:33,800 --> 00:23:35,200
Hey, Zoey, come out!

435
00:23:35,333 --> 00:23:36,600
Face us!

436
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:37,767
Zoey!

437
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:39,900
You know? I have an idea
who did this.

438
00:23:40,033 --> 00:23:42,633
Only one person knew
we were going there.

439
00:23:42,767 --> 00:23:44,000
Seems impossible.

440
00:23:44,133 --> 00:23:45,300
If not him, then who?

441
00:23:45,433 --> 00:23:47,500
That should serve as a lesson
to your brother.

442
00:23:47,633 --> 00:23:50,600
He should be careful
who he crosses.
